<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch10-17--grok> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch10-17: not-empirically-resolvable, resolvability 0.17";
    dc:description "The statement is a counterfactual about a meeting that the fossil record does not contain. Any real pattern of replacement is compatible with later forms being competitively superior and with later forms merely being different. Proxies require a substantial reinterpretation, so they do not resolve the claim as stated.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: The stated test is a competition, under a similar climate, between an extinct fauna or flora and a living one. No existing observation records the winner of that encounter, and modern invasions or trait trends change the contrast into a different question.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Competitive superiority is not a variable stored in occurrence or trait data without replacing the claim.", "Extinct species cannot be placed in competition with living ones.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.68"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasScore> "0.168"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasVerdict> "not-empirically-resolvable".
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch10-17--grok--analysis-feasibility> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/LLMClaimAssessment>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Analysis feasibility of darwin1859-ch10-17 by Grok 4.7: 0.2";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0-analysis-feasibility>;
